       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe and I want to check it with you first.\n\n**The problem:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily adds up to **6400 mg/day**.\n- The usual maximum single dose is **800 mg**.\n- The usual maximum daily dose is **3200 mg/day**, even under supervision.\n\nThis order would be twice the single-dose limit and twice the daily limit. That carries a high risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury and other toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n1. **Ibuprofen 400 mg by mouth four times daily** (1600 mg/day total). This is common if \"1600\" was the intended daily total.\n2. **Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3200 mg/day, the maximum).\n3. **Ibuprofen 600 mg by mouth four times daily** (2400 mg/day).\n4. Something else.\n\nTell me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away. If you really do mean 1600 mg per dose, please confirm and give the clinical reason, and I'll add a note to the order."
