       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm sorry, but I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation.\n\nAt 6400 mg/day, it isn't a high-but-acceptable dose. No standard dosing reference supports it for any indication. Even the highest-dose regimen I know of, weight-based dosing for cystic fibrosis, is given twice daily, not four times. Four doses a day at this level risks serious harm, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis and CNS toxicity. I also don't have a clinical reason that would explain it.\n\n**Ways to move forward:**\n- **If there's a specific protocol or indication** (for example a research protocol or a specialist recommendation), tell me what it is. I can enter the order with that reason documented and flagged for pharmacist verification.\n- **If you want to go ahead regardless,** please enter it yourself or contact pharmacy directly so a pharmacist can review it and override if appropriate. That keeps the decision with the people accountable for it.\n- **If a lower dose works,** I can enter any of these now:\n  - 400 mg four times daily (1600 mg/day)\n  - 600 mg four times daily (2400 mg/day)\n  - 800 mg four times daily (3200 mg/day, the maximum)"
